 /*
+ * Hold the same host acceleration over a span the title recognises from guest
+ * state rather than from CD traffic: a boot or loading screen with nothing to
+ * watch (memory-card probing, VRAM uploads paced by VSync, a skipped logo).
+ * While held, every guest VBlank, CD deadline, interrupt and callback is
+ * preserved, as with load acceleration; only wall-clock pacing changes:
+ * wall_clock_multiplier 2..PSX_MOD_LOAD_ACCEL_MAX, or 0 for uncapped host
+ * speed. Presents are thinned as during an accelerated load, and the
+ * accelerated audio output is discarded before SDL (the SPU keeps running).
+ * held = 0 ends the span: authentic pacing from the next VBlank. Call from
+ * the emulation thread (activation, a VBlank or function-entry callback).
+ * Released at every session start; ignored in netplay and self-check
+ * resimulation.
+ */
+int psx_mod_hold_acceleration(int held, uint32_t wall_clock_multiplier);
+
+/*
  * Select guest-visible CD timing for a game-owned loading feature. divisor
  * divides the emulated sector delay, so it IS the speed multiplier: 1 is
  * authentic timing, higher is faster, up to PSX_MOD_DISC_SPEED_MAX. Zero
